(1666890, 223849, 40718, '<td valign="top">I''m not too keen on military or gun pictures, but the composition of this Warthog is excellent.  The cannon is a little dark and maybe some dodging could bring out the individual barrels better.  7</td>', 'I''m not too keen on military or gun pictures, but the composition of this Warthog is excellent.  The cannon is a little dark and maybe some dodging could bring out the individual barrels better.  7', '2005-09-01 18:50:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(1666895, 223215, 40718, '<td valign="top">The combo is a little forced for the challenge...would you ever do this picture outside of D&amp;L?  However, the portrait is excellent and I gave it a 7 anyway.</td>', 'The combo is a little forced for the challenge...would you ever do this picture outside of D&L?  However, the portrait is excellent and I gave it a 7 anyway.', '2005-09-01 18:51:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1666921, 222767, 40718, '<td valign="top">Great colorful spider.  The OOF leg in front of the body is distracting.  If possible, I would have had the OOF leg be the one away from the body.  Could a different composition have achieved that?  I''m guessing you focused on the eyes and had the camera at the absolute minimum focal distance.  That will naturally blur the foreground images and sometimes shortens the DOF.  A small pullback from the minimum distance will give you a little extra DOF because you then get some foreground in focus rather than having it cut off immediately by the limitations of the lens.  (Does that make sense at all?  Am I just squawking?)  Anyway, 7.</td>', 'Great colorful spider.  The OOF leg in front of the body is distracting.  If possible, I would have had the OOF leg be the one away from the body.  Could a different composition have achieved that?  I''m guessing you focused on the eyes and had the camera at the absolute minimum focal distance.  That will naturally blur the foreground images and sometimes shortens the DOF.  A small pullback from the minimum distance will give you a little extra DOF because you then get some foreground in focus rather than having it cut off immediately by the limitations of the lens.  (Does that make sense at all?  Am I just squawking?)  Anyway, 7.', '2005-09-01 19:00:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1667009, 223711, 41872, '<td valign="top">I was looking through the photos to vote. I told myself I would vote for the one that made me say "Wow!" This one made me want to cry. Congrats. Great photograph.<br/></td>', 'I was looking through the photos to vote. I told myself I would vote for the one that made me say "Wow!" This one made me want to cry. Congrats. Great photograph.', '2005-09-01 19:27:13.000000', NULL, 1),
