(1676025, 223532, 17033, '<td valign="top">My opinion is that the key compositional element of this picture is that the mountain and the boat visually balance each other about the horizon. The use of a near-centre positioning enhances this aspect and so, IMO, you went down the right path rather than R.o.Thirds.</td>', 'My opinion is that the key compositional element of this picture is that the mountain and the boat visually balance each other about the horizon. The use of a near-centre positioning enhances this aspect and so, IMO, you went down the right path rather than R.o.Thirds.', '2005-09-05 13:52:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(1676028, 223730, 21216, '<td valign="top">Bang bang I was right ;) A very mesmerizing win.</td>', 'Bang bang I was right ;) A very mesmerizing win.', '2005-09-05 13:53:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(1676051, 223319, 30861, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Joey Lawrence:</b></div><hr/><i> Nice one bear, don''t be afraid to lean a bit more toward more editing. I''d really like to see more of the foreground brought out. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>If I were to print this image that''s what I''d do for sure, but it was shot for a challenge, the theme of the image is "darkness &amp; light", and I wanted a large, dark mass in the bottom and right of the image, which just a ghost of detail.</td>', 'Originally posted by Joey Lawrence: Nice one bear, don''t be afraid to lean a bit more toward more editing. I''d really like to see more of the foreground brought out.   If I were to print this image that''s what I''d do for sure, but it was shot for a challenge, the theme of the image is "darkness & light", and I wanted a large, dark mass in the bottom and right of the image, which just a ghost of detail.', '2005-09-05 14:02:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1676079, 223711, 27514, '<td valign="top">I define art as something that inspires or moves people emotionaly. I don''t think this photo does anything but inspires and moves me. great job, thank you so much for sharing this time in your life, a great story is told in this image. great job</td>', 'I define art as something that inspires or moves people emotionaly. I don''t think this photo does anything but inspires and moves me. great job, thank you so much for sharing this time in your life, a great story is told in this image. great job', '2005-09-05 14:13:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(1676087, 223267, 9821, '<td valign="top">there''s goes my top spot for this lens ... and I don''t own the lens anymore so i can''t reclaim it.<br/> <br/>...so i guess i''m happy for you ... and yet, still a bit sad :)<br/> <br/>congratulations<br/> <br/>ps ... i still have the 50mm 1.8 and 35mm 2.0 records, you don''t have one of those, do you?</td>', 'there''s goes my top spot for this lens ... and I don''t own the lens anymore so i can''t reclaim it. ...so i guess i''m happy for you ... and yet, still a bit sad :) congratulations ps ... i still have the 50mm 1.8 and 35mm 2.0 records, you don''t have one of those, do you?', '2005-09-05 14:15:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(1676123, 223814, 37200, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all for the comments.  This is only the second time I have attempted a self portrait, and yeah, not too comfortable with that process. :-)<br/> <br/>Since several of you asked, setup was a black sheet taped to a white wall.  Had a cheap clip light shining on the wall from the right to light that, and another one from the left to the side and slightly in front of where I was kneeling.  Camera on a tripod centered on the black/white line.  The rest was just touch-up in post (making the white, more white, adjusting the saturation, etc...).<br/></td>', 'Thanks to all for the comments.  This is only the second time I have attempted a self portrait, and yeah, not too comfortable with that process. :-) Since several of you asked, setup was a black sheet taped to a white wall.  Had a cheap clip light shining on the wall from the right to light that, and another one from the left to the side and slightly in front of where I was kneeling.  Camera on a tripod centered on the black/white line.  The rest was just touch-up in post (making the white, more white, adjusting the saturation, etc...).', '2005-09-05 14:32:28.000000', NULL, 0),
