(1676269, 223249, 93, '<td valign="top">Thought you''d retired :)  Ah well, look forward to seeing you fill up the Ds page, if anyone deserves to, you do.<br/> <br/>Happy DPCing.</td>', 'Thought you''d retired :)  Ah well, look forward to seeing you fill up the Ds page, if anyone deserves to, you do. Happy DPCing.', '2005-09-05 15:27:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(1676278, 223730, 24183, '<td valign="top">This photo is absolutly magnificent.  I can''t believe some people gave it a 1, its a 10 in my book.  I love the way you caught the light in her eyes.  It feels like she is right here with me.  Contgrats on another ribbon.  I am sure you are excited about the new challenge.<br/> <br/>Travis</td>', 'This photo is absolutly magnificent.  I can''t believe some people gave it a 1, its a 10 in my book.  I love the way you caught the light in her eyes.  It feels like she is right here with me.  Contgrats on another ribbon.  I am sure you are excited about the new challenge. Travis', '2005-09-05 15:30:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(1676286, 223878, 14414, '<td valign="top">beautiful photo, but i feel, as others have suggested, that a square crop might possibly be stronger? (cropping off top)</td>', 'beautiful photo, but i feel, as others have suggested, that a square crop might possibly be stronger? (cropping off top)', '2005-09-05 15:32:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(1676297, 223325, 37961, '<td valign="top">Congrats Dahkota! Met the challenge wonderfully and the mood is ever present.</td>', 'Congrats Dahkota! Met the challenge wonderfully and the mood is ever present.', '2005-09-05 15:36:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(1676307, 223325, 42792, '<td valign="top">This is such an amazing image.  I like how it''s as much art as it is a photo documentary of life as it exist for some (assume the graffiti and dirty corridor was in its natural state).</td>', 'This is such an amazing image.  I like how it''s as much art as it is a photo documentary of life as it exist for some (assume the graffiti and dirty corridor was in its natural state).', '2005-09-05 15:40:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(1676319, 223730, 93, '<td valign="top">Over smoothed, oversharpened, and yet still an 8.1<br/> <br/>Unbelievable.  Guess that''s the prize for being a recognizable and very well liked artist on this site.<br/> <br/>Of course, compositionally it is as great as ever, although I''d have loved to have seen a more colorful background. The black seems to really point out the over-sharpening where a more natural background may have helped hide it a little more.   Also, once again, would that I had a bank of "exotic" looking people to shoot.. seems to really make a punch with North Americans. <br/> <br/>Anyway, for me, a touch less of smoothing and sharpening would give this photo some real life.. <br/>Guess that''s why I usually don''t score well here.</td>', 'Over smoothed, oversharpened, and yet still an 8.1 Unbelievable.  Guess that''s the prize for being a recognizable and very well liked artist on this site. Of course, compositionally it is as great as ever, although I''d have loved to have seen a more colorful background. The black seems to really point out the over-sharpening where a more natural background may have helped hide it a little more.   Also, once again, would that I had a bank of "exotic" looking people to shoot.. seems to really make a punch with North Americans.  Anyway, for me, a touch less of smoothing and sharpening would give this photo some real life.. Guess that''s why I usually don''t score well here.', '2005-09-05 15:45:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(1676333, 223242, 93, '<td valign="top">Congratulations to the birth of your son :)</td>', 'Congratulations to the birth of your son :)', '2005-09-05 15:54:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(1676387, 223730, 13602, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Artyste:</b></div><hr/><i> Over smoothed, oversharpened, and yet still an 8.1<br/> <br/>Unbelievable.  Guess that''s the prize for being a recognizable and very well liked artist on this site.<br/> <br/>Of course, compositionally it is as great as ever, although I''d have loved to have seen a more colorful background. The black seems to really point out the over-sharpening where a more natural background may have helped hide it a little more.   Also, once again, would that I had a bank of "exotic" looking people to shoot.. seems to really make a punch with North Americans. <br/> <br/>Anyway, for me, a touch less of smoothing and sharpening would give this photo some real life.. <br/>Guess that''s why I usually don''t score well here. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>As I also commented during challenge, I completely agree with everything Artyste says. It''s a pitty that this site has become a "whoever is the most popular in the forums" wins. No offence intended to librodo, and nothing against him, it is the only image I commented in the challenge, that means it clearly triggered my attention, I really feel the image would be wonderful with regardless how much noise. Like this it looks like the poor girl is wrapped in a plastic bag, a manequin a doll anything but human. You have true talent it is obvious and it''s a pitty that you ruin your work just to please the DPC forums audience.<br/> <br/>However congrats for the ribbon.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-09-05 15:27:56.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Artyste: Over smoothed, oversharpened, and yet still an 8.1 Unbelievable.  Guess that''s the prize for being a recognizable and very well liked artist on this site. Of course, compositionally it is as great as ever, although I''d have loved to have seen a more colorful background. The black seems to really point out the over-sharpening where a more natural background may have helped hide it a little more.   Also, once again, would that I had a bank of "exotic" looking people to shoot.. seems to really make a punch with North Americans.  Anyway, for me, a touch less of smoothing and sharpening would give this photo some real life.. Guess that''s why I usually don''t score well here.   As I also commented during challenge, I completely agree with everything Artyste says. It''s a pitty that this site has become a "whoever is the most popular in the forums" wins. No offence intended to librodo, and nothing against him, it is the only image I commented in the challenge, that means it clearly triggered my attention, I really feel the image would be wonderful with regardless how much noise. Like this it looks like the poor girl is wrapped in a plastic bag, a manequin a doll anything but human. You have true talent it is obvious and it''s a pitty that you ruin your work just to please the DPC forums audience. However congrats for the ribbon.', '2005-09-05 16:21:26.000000', '2005-09-05 16:27:56.000000', 0),
