(1677426, 223730, 31813, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by frumoaznicul:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Artyste:</b></div><hr/><i> Over smoothed, oversharpened, and yet still an 8.1<br/> <br/>Unbelievable.  Guess that''s the prize for being a recognizable and very well liked artist on this site.<br/> <br/>Of course, compositionally it is as great as ever, although I''d have loved to have seen a more colorful background. The black seems to really point out the over-sharpening where a more natural background may have helped hide it a little more.   Also, once again, would that I had a bank of "exotic" looking people to shoot.. seems to really make a punch with North Americans. <br/> <br/>Anyway, for me, a touch less of smoothing and sharpening would give this photo some real life.. <br/>Guess that''s why I usually don''t score well here. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>As I also commented during challenge, I completely agree with everything Artyste says. It''s a pitty that this site has become a "whoever is the most popular in the forums" wins. No offence intended to librodo, and nothing against him, it is the only image I commented in the challenge, that means it clearly triggered my attention, I really feel the image would be wonderful with regardless how much noise. Like this it looks like the poor girl is wrapped in a plastic bag, a manequin a doll anything but human. You have true talent it is obvious and it''s a pitty that you ruin your work just to please the DPC forums audience.<br/> <br/>However congrats for the ribbon. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Agreed. <br/> <br/>"Nothing fails like success."<br/> <br/>JV</td>', 'Originally posted by frumoaznicul: Originally posted by Artyste: Over smoothed, oversharpened, and yet still an 8.1 Unbelievable.  Guess that''s the prize for being a recognizable and very well liked artist on this site. Of course, compositionally it is as great as ever, although I''d have loved to have seen a more colorful background. The black seems to really point out the over-sharpening where a more natural background may have helped hide it a little more.   Also, once again, would that I had a bank of "exotic" looking people to shoot.. seems to really make a punch with North Americans.  Anyway, for me, a touch less of smoothing and sharpening would give this photo some real life.. Guess that''s why I usually don''t score well here.   As I also commented during challenge, I completely agree with everything Artyste says. It''s a pitty that this site has become a "whoever is the most popular in the forums" wins. No offence intended to librodo, and nothing against him, it is the only image I commented in the challenge, that means it clearly triggered my attention, I really feel the image would be wonderful with regardless how much noise. Like this it looks like the poor girl is wrapped in a plastic bag, a manequin a doll anything but human. You have true talent it is obvious and it''s a pitty that you ruin your work just to please the DPC forums audience. However congrats for the ribbon.   Agreed.  "Nothing fails like success." JV', '2005-09-05 23:17:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(1677443, 223730, 13026, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Kaizen:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by frumoaznicul:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Artyste:</b></div><hr/><i> Over smoothed, oversharpened, and yet still an 8.1<br/> <br/>Unbelievable.  Guess that''s the prize for being a recognizable and very well liked artist on this site.<br/> <br/>Of course, compositionally it is as great as ever, although I''d have loved to have seen a more colorful background. The black seems to really point out the over-sharpening where a more natural background may have helped hide it a little more.   Also, once again, would that I had a bank of "exotic" looking people to shoot.. seems to really make a punch with North Americans. <br/> <br/>Anyway, for me, a touch less of smoothing and sharpening would give this photo some real life.. <br/>Guess that''s why I usually don''t score well here. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>As I also commented during challenge, I completely agree with everything Artyste says. It''s a pitty that this site has become a "whoever is the most popular in the forums" wins. No offence intended to librodo, and nothing against him, it is the only image I commented in the challenge, that means it clearly triggered my attention, I really feel the image would be wonderful with regardless how much noise. Like this it looks like the poor girl is wrapped in a plastic bag, a manequin a doll anything but human. You have true talent it is obvious and it''s a pitty that you ruin your work just to please the DPC forums audience.<br/> <br/>However congrats for the ribbon. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Agreed. <br/> <br/>"Nothing fails like success."<br/> <br/>JV </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I agree as well...And no offense at ALL to Manny, please don''t get me wrong.  I just think that, more often than not, if someone recognizes a popular photog''s work here on DPC, they will give it a high score, regardless of whether or not it is terribly creative or well done.  <br/> <br/>*shrugs*<br/> <br/>But yes.  Congratulationa on the ribbon, you do rock, librodo!  : )<br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Kaizen: Originally posted by frumoaznicul: Originally posted by Artyste: Over smoothed, oversharpened, and yet still an 8.1 Unbelievable.  Guess that''s the prize for being a recognizable and very well liked artist on this site. Of course, compositionally it is as great as ever, although I''d have loved to have seen a more colorful background. The black seems to really point out the over-sharpening where a more natural background may have helped hide it a little more.   Also, once again, would that I had a bank of "exotic" looking people to shoot.. seems to really make a punch with North Americans.  Anyway, for me, a touch less of smoothing and sharpening would give this photo some real life.. Guess that''s why I usually don''t score well here.   As I also commented during challenge, I completely agree with everything Artyste says. It''s a pitty that this site has become a "whoever is the most popular in the forums" wins. No offence intended to librodo, and nothing against him, it is the only image I commented in the challenge, that means it clearly triggered my attention, I really feel the image would be wonderful with regardless how much noise. Like this it looks like the poor girl is wrapped in a plastic bag, a manequin a doll anything but human. You have true talent it is obvious and it''s a pitty that you ruin your work just to please the DPC forums audience. However congrats for the ribbon.   Agreed.  "Nothing fails like success." JV   I agree as well...And no offense at ALL to Manny, please don''t get me wrong.  I just think that, more often than not, if someone recognizes a popular photog''s work here on DPC, they will give it a high score, regardless of whether or not it is terribly creative or well done.   *shrugs* But yes.  Congratulationa on the ribbon, you do rock, librodo!  : ) ', '2005-09-05 23:23:37.000000', NULL, 0),
