(1899977, 222719, 23471, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by DrAchoo:</b></div><hr/><i> I had no idea so many people would be curious about how I did this.  It was pretty simple really.  I hung a blank CD behind the candle and positioned the camera just right to capture a circular reflection.  It took a bit of goofing for the best exposure, but it wasn''t hard.  Thanks for all the comments... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>wow, that is absolutly genius.  well done!</td>', 'Originally posted by DrAchoo: I had no idea so many people would be curious about how I did this.  It was pretty simple really.  I hung a blank CD behind the candle and positioned the camera just right to capture a circular reflection.  It took a bit of goofing for the best exposure, but it wasn''t hard.  Thanks for all the comments...   wow, that is absolutly genius.  well done!', '2005-11-27 13:39:09.000000', NULL, 0),
